<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wales</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wales is a country of the United Kingdom on the western side of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardiff">Cardiff</a>. After Roman rule it was divided among Welsh kingdoms such as Gwynedd, Powys and Deheubarth, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-i-of-england">Edward I of England</a> conquered the last native principality in 1282–1283; the Laws in Wales Acts of 1535 and 1542 joined it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. It has had its own devolved parliament since 1999.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wales.jpg" alt="Wales" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown Vector graphics by Tobias Jakobs · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Wales.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
